"skill": [],
"responseType": "choice",
"question": "Which of the following figures made from 6 identical small squares cannot be folded into a cube?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "4 squares in a row, with 2 more below, directly adjoining the bottom edges of the 2 leftmost squares in that row (forming a 2-by-2 block)\n\n[Figure 1](figures/cnm_051_q4_choiceA_en.svg)",
"B": "3 squares in the first row and 3 in the second row, with the leftmost square of the second row directly adjoining the bottom edge of the rightmost square of the first row\n\n[Figure 2](figures/cnm_051_q4_choiceB_en.svg)",
"C": "3 rows of 2 squares each, with each row shifted one square to the right of the row above it, so that exactly one square in each pair of adjacent rows directly adjoins a square above or below\n\n[Figure 3](figures/cnm_051_q4_choiceC_en.svg)",
"D": "4 squares in the middle row, with 1 above and 1 below, directly adjoining the top and bottom, respectively, of a small square in the middle row\n\n[Figure 4](figures/cnm_051_q4_choiceD_en.svg)"
},
"choiceOrder": [
"A",
"B",
"C",
"D"
],
"choicesType": "figure",
"answer": "A",
"acceptedResponses": [
"A"
],
"rejectedAnswers": [],
"unorderedAnswers": false,
"solution": "A figure containing a \\(2\\times2\\) block cannot be folded into a cube (some faces would overlap). The other three are of types 3-3, 2-2-2, and 1-4-1, respectively, and are all nets of a cube.",
