"explanation": "The second equation has coefficient \\(1\\) on \\(x\\), so write \\(x=y+1\\). Substituting into the first equation leaves just \\(y\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{y+1}{2}+\\frac{y}{3}=3.\n\\]\nMultiply every term by \\(6\\) to clear the denominators:\n\\[\n3(y+1)+2y=18,\n\\qquad 5y+3=18.\n\\]\nThus \\(y=3\\) and \\(x=y+1=4\\). The answer is \\(4,3\\).",
