"responseType": "choice",
"question": "How do you construct the reflection of point \\(A\\) across line \\(l\\)?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "Through \\(A\\), draw a line parallel to \\(l\\), and mark off a segment of equal length on the other side of \\(l\\).",
"B": "Draw an arc centered at \\(A\\) with any radius, intersecting \\(l\\) at one point. That point is the required point.",
"C": "Join \\(A\\) to any point \\(P\\) on \\(l\\) and extend to \\(A'\\) so that \\(PA'=PA\\).",
"D": "Through \\(A\\), draw a perpendicular to \\(l\\), with foot \\(O\\). On the perpendicular on the other side, mark \\(A'\\) so that \\(OA'=OA\\). Then \\(A'\\) is the required point."
},
