"id": "cnm_135_q3_m2",
"label": "Use preservation of length",
"explanation": "Reflection preserves segment lengths, so we can find \\(AB\\) without locating the reflected points. Because \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) lie on the same horizontal line on opposite sides of the vertical line \\(l\\), their perpendicular distances to \\(l\\) form the two parts of \\(AB\\). Therefore,\n\\[\nA'B'=AB=3+2=5.\n\\]\nThe length is \\(5\\) grid squares.",
