"label": "Square symmetry and an attainable bound",
"explanation": "\\(B\\) and \\(D\\) are reflections of each other across \\(AC\\), so \\(PB=PD\\). Thus, \\(PB+PE=PD+PE\\geq DE\\), and \\(DE=\\sqrt{8^2+6^2}=10\\).\n\nSegment \\(DE\\) lies within the square and joins points on opposite sides of diagonal \\(AC\\), so it intersects segment \\(AC\\). Choosing \\(P\\) at this intersection gives \\(PD+PE=DE=10\\), so the minimum value of \\(PB+PE\\) is \\(10\\).",
