"explanation": "The given sum and difference let us find \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) by eliminating one variable. Adding the equations gives \\(2a=7\\), so \\(a=\\frac{7}{2}\\). Subtracting the second equation from the first gives \\(2b=3\\), so \\(b=\\frac{3}{2}\\). Therefore\n\\[\na^2-b^2=\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^2-\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2=\\frac{49-9}{4}=10.\n\\]",
