"label": "Factor, convert, and substitute",
"explanation": "Since \\(x^2-x=x(x-1)\\) and \\(x^2-1=(x-1)(x+1)\\), the least common denominator is \\(P=x(x-1)(x+1)\\). For \\(x\\ne -1,0,1\\), multiply the first fraction's numerator and denominator by \\(x+1\\), and the second fraction's by \\(x\\), to obtain the common denominator:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{x^2-x}=\\frac{x+1}{P},\\qquad\n\\frac{1}{x^2-1}=\\frac{x}{P}.\n\\]\nWhen \\(x=3\\), \\(P=3\\times2\\times4=24\\).",
