"label": "Find the triangle's height",
"explanation": "The diagonals bisect each other, so \\(O\\) is the midpoint of \\(AC\\). Let \\(M\\) be the midpoint of \\(AB\\). In \\(\\triangle ABC\\), the segment \\(OM\\) joins two side midpoints, so \\(OM\\parallel BC\\) and \\(OM=BC/2=4\\). Since \\(BC\\perp AB\\), \\(OM\\) is the height of \\(\\triangle OAB\\) above base \\(AB\\). Its area is therefore\n\\[\n\\frac12 AB\\cdot OM=\\frac12\\cdot6\\cdot4=12.\n\\]",
