"label": "Complete the square",
"explanation": "Rearranging gives \\(x^2-4x=1\\). Adding \\((4/2)^2=4\\) to both sides gives \\((x-2)^2=5\\), so \\(x=2\\pm\\sqrt{5}\\). A's right-hand side is incorrect because adding \\(4\\) to \\(1\\) gives \\(5\\), not \\(3\\). B has a sign error, and D adds the wrong number when completing the square. The correct choice is C.",
