"explanation": "A given root makes the equation zero, so substituting \\(x=2\\) determines \\(k\\):\n\\[\n4+2k+6=0,\\qquad 2k=-10,\\qquad k=-5.\n\\]\nWith this value, the equation becomes\n\\[\nx^2-5x+6=(x-2)(x-3)=0.\n\\]\nIts roots are \\(2\\) and \\(3\\), so the other root is \\(3\\). The requested pair is \\(-5,\\,3\\).",
