"explanation": "The figures before and after a rotation are congruent, so corresponding line segments are equal in length and corresponding angles are equal.\n\nThis makes A true. Equal corresponding lengths are also proportional with common ratio \\(1\\): if corresponding segment lengths are \\(\\ell>0\\) and \\(\\ell'\\), then \\(\\ell'=\\ell\\), so \\(\\ell'/\\ell=1\\). Thus B is true as well. C is not a general rotation property; for example, a \\(60^\\circ\\) angle remains \\(60^\\circ\\), and these two angles are not supplementary. Therefore A and B both hold, so the keyed A is not the unique correct choice.",
