"label": "Count from both ends",
"explanation": "A chord is determined by its two endpoints. Each of the six points can be joined to the other five, giving \\(6\\times5=30\\) counts. Every chord is counted twice, once from each end, so joining all pairs gives\n\\[\n\\frac{6\\times5}{2}=15\n\\]\ndistinct chords. Since every pair is allowed, the maximum is \\(15\\).",
