"label": "Use the major arc directly",
"explanation": "The opposite vertices \\(A\\) and \\(C\\) lie on opposite arcs with endpoints \\(B,D\\). Since \\(A\\) lies on the major arc \\(BD\\), \\(C\\) lies on the minor arc, so \\(\\angle C\\) intercepts the major arc. This arc measures \\(360^\\circ-140^\\circ=220^\\circ\\). By the inscribed angle theorem,\n\\[\n\\angle C=\\frac{220^\\circ}{2}=110^\\circ.\n\\]",
