"label": "Calculate with the variance convention stated",
"explanation": "If sample variance is defined as the mean of the squared differences from the mean, divide by the sample size \\(5\\). Using the given mean \\(94\\), A's variance is\n\\[\n\\frac{16+4+0+4+16}{5}=8,\n\\]\nand B's variance is\n\\[\n\\frac{4+1+0+1+4}{5}=2.\n\\]\nThe difference is \\(8-2=6\\text{ cm}^2\\), indicating that the sampled heights in A are less uniform.\n\nThe displayed question does not specify the divisor. Under the convention that divides by \\(5-1=4\\), the same squared-deviation totals give\n\\[\n\\frac{40}{4}-\\frac{10}{4}=7.5\\text{ cm}^2.\n\\]\nThus the answer is \\(6\\) with divisor \\(5\\), or \\(7.5\\) with divisor \\(4\\); the wording does not select a unique answer.",
