"label": "Complete the square",
"explanation": "The fixed sum lets us write \\(y=10-x\\), with \\(0<x<10\\) because both numbers are positive. Completing the square expresses the product as a constant minus a square:\n\\[\nxy=x(10-x)=25-(x-5)^2\\le25.\n\\]\nThe square is zero at \\(x=5\\), giving \\(y=5\\). This pair is allowed, so the maximum is \\(25\\).",
