"responseType": "numeric",
"question": "What is the larger real root of the equation \\(x^2-5x+6=0\\)?",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {},
"choiceOrder": [],
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "3",
"acceptedResponses": [
"3"
],
"rejectedAnswers": [],
"unorderedAnswers": false,
"solution": "Because \\(2+3=5\\) and \\(2\\cdot3=6\\), the equation factors as\n\\[\n(x-2)(x-3)=0.\n\\]\nA product is zero exactly when at least one factor is zero, so \\(x-2=0\\) or \\(x-3=0\\). The two roots are 2 and 3, and the larger one is 3.",
