"id": "square-sum-identity",
"label": "Use the square-sum identity",
"explanation": "The square-sum identity lets us find sine without first finding the angle. Since \\(\\cos\\theta=1\\),\n\\[\\sin^2\\theta=1-\\cos^2\\theta=1-1^2=0.\\]\nThe only real number whose square is zero is zero, so \\(\\sin\\theta=0\\).",
