"id": "unit-circle-reflection",
"label": "Reflect the unit-circle point",
"explanation": "For any real angle \\(\\alpha\\), its unit-circle point is \\((\\cos\\alpha,\\sin\\alpha)\\). Reflection across the \\(y\\)-axis changes its direction angle to \\(180^\\circ-\\alpha\\), up to a whole number of turns, and changes its coordinates to \\((-\\cos\\alpha,\\sin\\alpha)\\). Cosine is the horizontal coordinate, so\n\\[\\cos(180^\\circ-\\alpha)=-\\cos\\alpha.\\]\nThus C is correct for every real \\(\\alpha\\).",
