"label": "Equal legs in a right triangle",
"explanation": "For \\(0^\\circ<x<90^\\circ\\), represent \\(x\\) as an acute angle of a right triangle. Tangent is the opposite leg divided by the adjacent leg, so \\(\\tan x=1\\) means the two positive leg lengths are equal. Their opposite angles are equal and sum to \\(90^\\circ\\), giving \\(2x=90^\\circ\\) and \\(x=45^\\circ\\). Conversely, equal legs give \\(\\tan45^\\circ=1\\). If the endpoints are included, \\(\\tan0^\\circ=0\\) and \\(\\tan90^\\circ\\) is undefined. Thus the only answer in degrees is \\(45\\).",
