"rejectedAnswers": [],
"unorderedAnswers": false,
"solution": "Assume, as in the recorded qualification, that \\(\\omega\\ne0\\) and the time domain contains a point where \\(\\sin(\\omega t)=1\\). The maximum value of sine is \\(1\\), so the highest temperature is \\(10+8=18\\).\n\nThe time-domain condition matters. For example, if \\(\\omega=1\\) and \\(\\pi\\le t\\le2\\pi\\), then \\(\\sin t\\le0\\), with equality at the endpoints, so the highest temperature is \\(10\\). If the nonconstant assumption is also dropped, \\(\\omega=0\\) gives the constant temperature \\(10\\).\n\nThus \\(18\\) is the intended answer under the recorded assumptions; without them, the highest temperature is not uniquely determined.",
