"id": "cnm_h085_q4_m2",
"label": "Compare coordinates",
"explanation": "The given coordinate vectors let us determine every possible coefficient pair directly. If \\((3,5)=a e_1+b e_2\\), where \\(a,b\\) are real numbers, then\n\\[\n(3,5)=a(1,0)+b(0,1)=(a,b).\n\\]\nComparing components forces \\(a=3\\) and \\(b=5\\), and this pair satisfies the equation. Hence the decomposition is unique, making B true. Both forced coefficients are positive, so D also holds for the specified vector and basis. The single-choice answer is therefore ambiguous between B and D.",
