"solution": "A square has equal sides, but this does not specify their numerical length or their direction relative to the drawing axes.\n\nAssume conditionally that the square has side length \\(s>0\\), its sides follow the original planar axes, and the usual oblique dimetric convention applies. A side parallel to the original \\(y\\)-axis is drawn at half length, \\(s/2\\), while a side parallel to the original \\(x\\)-axis keeps length \\(s\\). In the half-scale direction, squares with side lengths \\(4\\) and \\(6\\) therefore give drawn lengths \\(2\\) and \\(3\\). Even with side length \\(4\\), a requested side in the unscaled direction would have drawn length \\(4\\).\n\nThe displayed question supplies neither the side length nor the identified direction, and no figure supplies them. Thus no unique numerical answer follows. The recorded key \\(2\\) is recovered if the missing setup specifies side length \\(4\\) and the requested side in the half-scale direction; grading must remain withheld.",
