"id": "cnm_h117_q1_m2",
"label": "Use coplanarity and nonintersection",
"explanation": "Both \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) lie in the cutting plane, so they are coplanar. Since \\(a\\parallel\\alpha\\), no point of \\(a\\) lies in \\(\\alpha\\). But \\(b\\) lies in \\(\\alpha\\), so \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) have no common point. Coplanar lines with no common point are parallel. Thus \\(a\\parallel b\\), choice C.",
