"label": "Count by the smaller label",
"explanation": "Label the items \\(1,2,\\ldots,10\\). Count each pair according to its smaller label: label \\(1\\) has \\(9\\) possible larger partners, label \\(2\\) has \\(8\\), and so on down to label \\(9\\), which has \\(1\\). Every two-item selection has exactly one smaller label, so these cases include every selection exactly once. Thus the number of selections is\n\\[\n9+8+7+6+5+4+3+2+1=45.\n\\]",
