"label": "Complete the square",
"explanation": "Both side lengths must be positive, so \\(0<x<12\\). Writing the area as a constant minus a square makes its upper bound visible:\n\\[\nS=x(24-2x)=72-2(x-6)^2\\le72.\n\\]\nEquality holds exactly when \\(x=6\\), which lies in the allowed interval. Thus the area is greatest when \\(x=6\\) meters.",
